STATEMENT: >>>
Grammar to load: `tree-sitter-grammars.tree-sitter-typescript` (nixpkgs, 0.23.2, `python313Packages`/`python314Packages` binding present). TSX is a second, separate nixpkgs attribute from the same upstream repo, `tree-sitter-grammars.tree-sitter-tsx` (0.23.2, binding present) — TypeScript and TSX are two distinct grammars, not one grammar with a mode flag, so a `.tsx` extractor needs the second attribute even though this repo has no `.tsx` file today.

Candidate items (node type, confirmed against upstream `tree-sitter/tree-sitter-typescript`'s `typescript/src/node-types.json`): `interface_declaration`, `type_alias_declaration`, `class_declaration`, `function_declaration`, `enum_declaration`, `method_definition` (inside a class body), and `export_statement` as the wrapper a top-level declaration is commonly found under (`export interface Foo {}` parses as `export_statement` wrapping `interface_declaration`).

Present in this repo today: 4 files, `overlays/kiro-memory-distiller/{distiller,distiller.test}.ts` and `overlays/mcp-servers/openmemory-mem/{openmemory-mem,openmemory-mem.test}.ts` — two source/test pairs, both MCP-adjacent overlay update tooling.

Gap: no forcing function today at 4 files, but the operator has named this the target language for a pending JS rewrite (see NOTES), so the grammar and item set above should be treated as ready-to-adopt rather than speculative.
